00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,080
Listen to a talk in an anthropology class.

2
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:05,864
Man:

3
00:00:05,864 --> 00:00:09,844
Often when we think of mummies, we think of ancient Egyptians

4
00:00:09,844 --> 00:00:13,160
and their elaborate methods of preserving bodies.

5
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:20,216
We used to think Egyptians were the only people practicing mummification during the Bronze

6
00:00:20,216 --> 00:00:23,623
Age, about, oh, 4000 years ago,

7
00:00:23,623 --> 00:00:31,280
because typical mummies are found in places, for example, with very dry climates like Egypt.

8
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:39,090
But then archaeologists discovered a site in Scotland with evidence of mummification.

9
00:00:39,090 --> 00:00:44,200
And Scotland is, well, wet, rainy.

10
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:51,241
This site is called Cladh Hallan, the only place in Britain where we found

11
00:00:51,241 --> 00:00:54,150
prehistoric Bronze Age mummies.

12
00:00:54,150 --> 00:01:00,349
So researchers unearthed skeletons at Cladh Hallan, including a man

13
00:01:00,349 --> 00:01:04,140
and a woman from around 1500 BCE.

14
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:12,180
Since these were just skeletons, the researchers didn't realize at first that they had actually been mummies.

15
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:20,000
That realization came after doing a test called radiocarbon dating on the bones.

16
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:28,170
Radiocarbon dating revealed that the man and woman had died several hundred years before being buried.

17
00:01:28,170 --> 00:01:33,927
Normally, such a long wait would turn a body into a pile of bones,

18
00:01:33,927 --> 00:01:38,100
not an actual skeleton like what was found.

19
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:45,160
So their bodies must have been purposely preserved for hundreds of years before burial.

20
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,551
Why?

21
00:01:46,551 --> 00:01:49,070
Well, who knows?

22
00:01:49,070 --> 00:01:51,060
But we do know how.

23
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:57,050
The bodies were preserved, mummified in a peat bog.

24
00:01:57,050 --> 00:02:04,470
Peat bogs are kind of like swamps, except their conditions prevent organic materials like

25
00:02:04,470 --> 00:02:07,120
bodies from fully breaking down.

26
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:10,000
They stay more intact.

27
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:17,826
Prehistoric people in Scotland used to preserve animal fat like butter in peat bogs,

28
00:02:17,826 --> 00:02:21,180
so they definitely had the concept.
